  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Action Roll",
    "section": "6.2",
    "heading": "1. The Player States Their Goal",
    "lineStart": 320,
    "lineEnd": 324
  },
  "section": "6.2",
  "rulesText": "Your goal is the concrete outcome your character will achieve when they overcome the obstacle at hand. Usually the character's goal is pretty obvious in context, but it's the GM's job to ask and clarify the goal when necessary.\n\n*\"You're punching him in the face, right? Okay... what do want to get out of this? Do you want to take him out, or just rough him up so he'll do what you want?\"*"
}
